#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068577 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4682b115-6156-5496-8faf-81000bcd993e" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Difference of Cubes"}] :question/id #uuid "eb4964f1-0462-5a41-b712-3d0d4dbd8c1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4967" :question/problem "Factor $x^3 - 8$." :question/worked-solution "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\na^3-b^3=(a-b)(a^2+ab+b^2)\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write the given expression as a difference of cubes:\n\n$$\nx^3 - 8 = x^3 - 2^3\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the given expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} x^3 - 8 & = x^3 - 2^3 \\\\[3pt] & = (x - 2)\\left(x^2 + 2\\cdot x + 2^2\\right) \\\\[3pt] & = (x - 2)\\left(x^2 + 2x + 4\\right) \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb1e753f-ed91-5ba4-bd25-5fba48060d58" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Sum of Cubes"}] :question/id #uuid "c0f5e363-d4cd-5e31-bd25-6825209d58d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-4968" :question/problem "Factor $8n^3 + m^6$." :question/worked-solution "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\na^3+b^3=(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2)\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n8n^3 + m^6 = (2n)^3 + (m^2)^3\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8n^{3} + m^{6} &= (2n)^{3} + (m^{2})^{3} \\\\\n&= (2n + m^{2})((2n)^{2} - 2n \\cdot m^{2} + (m^{2})^{2}) \\\\\n&= (2n + m^{2})(4n^{2} - 2m^{2}n + m^{4})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "979f1a29-d9b2-50f1-9bef-252125d1021f" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring Sums and Differences of Cubes with Fractional Terms"}] :question/id #uuid "e90d590d-956d-5bb7-af6c-7572051b7f1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4969" :question/problem "Factor $1 - \\dfrac 1 {t^9}$." :question/worked-solution "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\na^3-b^3=(a-b)(a^2+ab+b^2)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n1 - \\dfrac{1}{t^9} = 1^3 - \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t^3}\\right)^3\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - \\frac{1}{t^{9}} &= 1^{3} - (\\frac{1}{t^{3}})^{3} \\\\\n&= (1 - \\frac{1}{t^{3}})(1^{2} + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{t^{3}} + (\\frac{1}{t^{3}})^{2}) \\\\\n&= (1 - \\frac{1}{t^{3}})(1 + \\frac{1}{t^{3}} + (1)/((t^{3})^{2})) \\\\\n&= (1 - \\frac{1}{t^{3}})(1 + \\frac{1}{t^{3}} + \\frac{1}{t^{6}})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
